[Music]  imagine an alternate world where  dinosaurs evolved intelligence  comparable to a human's what might these  intelligent dinosaurs look like what  kind of technology culture and art might  they produce this speculative timeline  is the subject of dinosauroids a  world-building project conceptualized in  part by siam kozaman whose work you may  know from his sci-fi book all tomorrows  or from his speculative paleontology  book all yesterdays the latter of which  i've got a video on elsewhere in the  archive dinosauroids also comes from  simon roy an accomplished comic book  artist and writer who created much of  the art you'll see in this video these  two are outstanding creators and i have  links to where you can follow and  support them in this video's description  the dinosauroids project was born in  part out of cozamans and roy's  frustration with the work of  paleontologist dale russell who in 1982  created this concept of how a species  like atrodon might evolve into an  upright walking bipedal organism with  human-like intelligence while the  depiction has a retro vibe i find kind  of entertaining it's a pretty  old-fashioned and human-centric model of  an intelligent dinosaur so kozeman and  roy created their own more  scientifically viable models which don't  look much like humans but of all the  right ingredients for human-like  intelligence so for this entry into the  archive we'll explore the incredibly  detailed speculative world in history  roy and kozman created to go alongside  these new dinosaurs they even imagine  incredibly the art these creatures might  produce which we'll get into later in  the video  with that said let's begin  in the hypothetical alternate timeline  of dinosauroids there was no end  cretaceous asteroid impact nor did any  other cataclysm befall the non-avian  dinosaurs kozaman and roy theorized that  even without a mass extinction dinosaur  groups would have kept evolving into new  unfamiliar forms for now let's focus on  the dinosauroids themselves and explore  how the authors speculate they might  have first evolved the species they  imagine originated from troadon-like  ancestors the development of their  advanced intelligence and early use of  tools likely began slowly while the very  image of a bird-like species using  primitive spears might seem surprising  to some various modern birds in  particular crows which inspired the look  of dinosauroids are highly intelligent  and have indeed been seen using simple  tools and solving logical puzzles in  this experiment from the university of  auckland you can see a crow using stones  to gain access to submerged food showing  an impressive understanding of water  displacement in the process so the idea  of a bird-like dinosaur achieving  advanced intelligence through a similar  foundation isn't too outside the realm  of possibility  this image illustrates the two species  of intelligent dinosaurs on this  alternate earth both of which diverge  from a troidon-like ancestor while the  idea of multiple intelligent species  living on one planet at the same time  might seem surprising it's not too far  off from our own history with humans and  neanderthals the hypothetical scientific  designations of the two dinosauroids are  avisapians sorotheos and avasapian  statoricus and while both species make  frequent use of their beaks for tool use  they also seem to have complex hands  with dexterous fingers a feature that  could allow them to make use of delicate  tools and evolve brain function  analogous to a human's  aside from the dinosauroids the authors  designed an extensive ecosystem of  animals around the titular species while  most of these dinosaurs are descendants  of the manoraptorin group koziman and  roy also populated this hypothetical  world with various species of mammals  which have managed to grow into large  and sophisticated forms just like in our  time despite the presence of dinosaurs  due to the butterfly effect however  these mammals would of course be  different from the species we're  familiar with even if there are some  parallels one entertaining example of a  new species is the mega tapiris a large  herbivore that superficially resembles  an elephant due to the honing force of  convergent evolution a neat idea the  authors also imagine a variety of  mammalian carnivores that somewhat  resemble canine predators these mammals  are far from the largest organisms  patrolling this hypothetical world  however which still very much belongs to  the dinosaurs on the subject of  dinosaurs the authors wanted pterosaurs  to fill various niches since these  species were already in decline by the  time of the asteroid's impact however  kozaman and roy have imagined them  dwindling down to just a few subspecies  comparable to storks and other large  water birds  in terms of larger dinosaurs we have the  aptly named classification of the avid  titans massive lumbering herbivores that  are the largest new organisms on this  alternate earth another large species is  the bull bird a wary and dangerous  scavenger that stalks the plains of the  eurasian continent kozaman and roy  imagined that hunting bull birds was a  rite of passage for early dinosauroids  who needed to coordinate with each other  to take the beasts down some hunters  enlisted the help of jackal birds  hawk-like species that the dinosauroids  inventively managed to domesticate just  like early humans and the ancestor of  the modern dog but dinosauroids and  their domestic pets aren't the only  hunters on the plains these are the  tyranna raptors a species of  hypothetical theropods whose evolution  echoes that of none other than the  massive jawed tyrannosaurus rex this  dangerous predator is also known by the  dinosaurs as black thing and are the  largest predators in this imagined  dominion  in order to survive in this dangerous  world dinosauroids the creators  speculate have had to rely on their  technological cunning much like early  humans here you can see a dinosauroid  with a carved stone tool in its mouth  used for hunting at this point in the  speculative timeline most tribes of  dinosauroids are nomadic building  temporary structures while migrating for  protection from the elements one detail  i like is that these structures look a  lot like the nests of modern birds which  don't forget are also descendants of  theropods the authors imagine that the  dinosauroids do eventually form more  permanent village-like settlements which  are intriguingly still made up of nest  houses just more sturdy ones in these  more permanent societies early forms of  intricate cultural expression might  emerge like this young artist painting  on stretched animal skins using ground  up soil as well as other natural  pigments and a brush made from a wing  feather pretty clever still many  dinosaurs maintain migratory lifestyles  like these two individuals with a  domesticated form of bull bird mentioned  previously which is carrying their  various supplies other dinosauroids  travel light like this mountaineering  duo carrying weapons and travel gear  themselves curiously roy and koziman  mentioned their weapons are crafted from  bronze indicating the dinosauroids are  emerging into a new phase of  technological development many groups  also seem to equip themselves with  weaponized war masks wooden helmet-like  structures with obsidian blade edges to  improve the striking power of their  beaks while these masked warriors look  imposing the authors imagine these masks  while intimidating aren't actually the  most practical but dinosaurs society is  clearly becoming more technologically  proficient inventing armaments like a  unique spear-throwing device and  primitive bronze age sets of armor  clearly the dinosauroids are for better  or worse following our own path in many  ways  but warfare isn't the only aspect of  dinosauroid culture that kozman and roy  have fleshed out the two have also  created various images depicting what  paintings by dinosauroids might look  like  take for example this painting depicting  an eva titan family here the broad  impressionistic strokes that are a  trademark of the dinosauroid style are  reflective of how they use feathers to  apply paint or take this stylized  painting of a dinosauroid hunter  spearing some four-legged mammal an  image which reminds me of early cave  paintings are human ancestors created  even more stylized we have a mural of a  warrior confronting a spirit creature  here you can see elements of myths and  legends sneaking their way into the art  just as was the case with human cultural  development the dangerous predatory  black thing gets a similar treatment  with the organism's mouth and horns  exaggerated in the artist's recreation  reflecting the parts of the animal that  stood out the most to the dinosauroid  creator  and beyond paintings perhaps the  dinosauroids might have also told spoken  stories and their own bird-like  languages here you can see a fireside  chat between an elder and several  hatchlings kozaman and roy imagine this  storyteller is weaving tales of spirits  and other worlds in particular a legend  of a sky god which resembles a flying  pterosaur what a creative level of world  building beyond these early societies  who knows what the future might have  held for a species like the dinosauroids  perhaps their technology would continue  to develop like this hypothetical sketch  of a more heavily armored warrior which  almost resembles a knight and who knows  perhaps long into the hypothetical  future this species might even develop  the technology necessary to become a  space-faring civilization it's a pretty  interesting concept although not one  kosman and roy have said they've pursued  seriously still the hypothetical future  of the dinosauroids seems full of  endless potential although we've reached  the end of our exploration for this  particular video if you like this world  please consider supporting roy and  kozmin by patronizing their other works  and social media which as always you can  find in the links below and if you like  this video i have others covering the  speculative work of cm kozumin elsewhere  in the archive also thanks for watching  if you enjoyed this entry please lend  your support and like subscribe and hit  the notification icon to stay up to date  on all things curious see you in the  next video  i

